<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Without loss of generality, we may suppose that $K$ is an $\infty $-category. Let $\widetilde{K} \rightarrow K$ be a left fibration classified by $F$. Since $F$ is corepresentable, $\widetilde{K}$ has an initial object and is therefore weakly contractible. Corollary <a href="/tag/ADD452" data-tag="ADD452">3.3.4.6</a> implies that there is an isomorphism $\widetilde{K} \simeq X$ in the homotopy category $\calH $, so that $X$ is also contractible. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>